Show "Restore pages?" only while the last session's crash is pending

After the user restored (or closed the bubble, or used a new window), a
window opened later through the startup path (running chromium again, a
launcher) offered to restore again: HasPendingUncleanExit() relied on
ProfileLaunchObserver, which forgets the launched profiles once startup
is done. Also require ExitTypeService to still wait for the crash to be
acknowledged.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/startup/startup_browser_creator.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/startup/startup_browser_creator.cc
index be05049..59f2ae1 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/startup/startup_browser_creator.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/startup/startup_browser_creator.cc
@@ -1596,8 +1596,16 @@ bool StartupBrowserCreator::ActivatedProfile() {
 }
 
 bool HasPendingUncleanExit(Profile* profile) {
+  // Once the user has acknowledged the crash (restored, closed the bubble or
+  // used a new window), the last session's crash is no longer pending: don't
+  // offer to restore it again in later windows. ProfileLaunchObserver forgets
+  // the launched profiles once startup is done, so it can't tell.
+  ExitTypeService* exit_type_service =
+      ExitTypeService::GetInstanceForProfile(profile->GetOriginalProfile());
   return ExitTypeService::GetLastSessionExitType(profile) ==
              ExitType::kCrashed &&
+         exit_type_service &&
+         exit_type_service->waiting_for_user_to_ack_crash() &&
          !ProfileLaunchObserver::HasBeenLaunchedAndBrowserOpen(profile) &&
          !base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->HasSwitch(
              switches::kHideCrashRestoreBubble);
